A||N||8||terryk||84 Glass Sail Panels on 86SE?||||1||
Z||000000||terryk||04-02-2000||02:57 PM||||Can I install a set of 84 SE glass sail panels on an 86SE (replacing the cracked plastic panels)?<P>Anyone done this?<P>I know, search the archives...........||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||04-02-2000||03:57 PM||||I'm pretty sure that the 84 panels mount in a different way.. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||04-02-2000||06:21 PM||||The 84's can likely be moved. I believe you'll need to strip the interior trim and drill holes.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Old Lar||04-02-2000||07:03 PM||||I don't think the sail panels are the same size for 86 as 84.   Take lots of measurments||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||04-02-2000||07:56 PM||||I thought both the glass and plastic where held on with two 10mm nuts and two clips in the same location.<P>Looking at the 86 manual, it looks like it mounts exactly like the 84 glass. What am I missing?<p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 04-02-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||fieroshop||04-02-2000||08:11 PM||||Terry, all you have to do is remove the interior trim along going up the door jamb. Next make sure you use the clips from the 84 panels and make sure you tighten the 11mm nuts that are inside the door post. I have installed many of these panels and I try to get all I can get from the wrecking yards. I sell these for $30.00 ea. So go for it, they look better then the plastic panels and will last the lifetime of the car.||||reg||1
Z||000006||terryk||04-02-2000||08:30 PM||||Thanks Fieroshop (if that's your *real* name!) <P>That's what I suspected. The glass cleans up nicely. Too bad there wasn't a glass GT panel.<P>What's the difference in the clips?||||reg||14
Z||000008||Oreif||04-02-2000||09:21 PM||||I have an 86 SE and I have 84 SE glass q-windows installed. There is no drilling or modification required. You do have to use the Clips that come with the 84 ones. The clips mount to the glass differently then the plstic q-windows but the clips mount to the body the same. The stud that you heve to tighten from inside is part of the glass. DO NOT OVER TIGHTEN the glass will crack. If you buy the glass ones, Clean them real good before mounting. I even purchased the red and silver new Pontiac emblems for them. They look brand new! ||||reg||4
Z||000009||terryk||04-02-2000||09:45 PM||||Great info oefir, I have to do two cars. The glass one's are in good shape. The gasket needs some trim black though.||||reg||1
